        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: സാക്ഷി",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "സാക്ഷി — sākṣi — \"a witness\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "അപകടം കണ്ട സാക്ഷി പോലീസിനോട് സംസാരിച്ചു. apakaṭaṁ kaṇṭa sākṣi pōlīsinōṭŭ saṁsāriccu. The witness who saw the accident spoke to the police."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Plural: സാക്ഷികൾ. To give evidence is സാക്ഷി (sākṣi) പറയുക, literally to say as a witness."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "സാക്ഷി (sākṣi) is borrowed from Sanskrit sākṣin, \"a witness\" (CDIAL 13321). CDIAL takes the Sanskrit word apart as sa- \"with\" and akṣi \"eye\": the witness is the one who was there with his own eyes."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling what happened."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
