          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "യുദ്ധം — yuddhaṁ — \"a war; a battle\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ആ യുദ്ധം വളരെ കാലം മുൻപ് നടന്നു. ā yuddhaṁ vaḷare kālaṁ munpŭ naṭannu. That war took place a very long time ago."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "With ചെയ്യുക it makes a verb: യുദ്ധം (yuddhaṁ) ചെയ്യുക, to fight a war."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "യുദ്ധം (yuddhaṁ) is borrowed from Sanskrit yuddha, \"fought\", and as a noun \"a battle\", the past participle of the root yudh, \"to fight\" (CDIAL 10499). Like many Sanskrit nouns in -a, it ends in -ം in Malayalam."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
